            <ArticleTitle>Epicardial adipose tissue thickness in young Indian overweight and obese individuals.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S56-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/2141-9248.131720</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Epicardial adipose tissue (EAT) has been found to be an important reliable marker for future coronary events. Deposition of the EAT in young individuals is not well known. We studied EAT in 25 young overweight or obese individuals. In spite of the high visceral fat and total body fat, EAT thickness was not found to be high in the participants of our study.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
